    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "After 37837ff commit (which started to use Lua callbacks as right hand side of mappings where reasonable), 'mini.ai' doesn't work in Visual mode with 'which-key.nvim'.\r\n\r\nSymptoms:\r\n- 'mini.ai' works in Operator-pending mode, but not in Visual. For example: `daf` works, but `vaf` does not.\r\n- Works without 'which-key.nvim', but does not work with it.\r\n\r\nThe core reason seems to be an upstream issue: folke/which-key.nvim#449.\r\n\r\nHere are the ways to make it work:\r\n- Update 'which-key.nvim', as its issue is fixed on version 1.4.1..\r\n- Add `triggers_blacklist = { v = { 'a', 'i' } }` to `require('which-key').setup()` call.\r\n- Run `require('which-key').setup()` *before* `require('mini.ai').setup()` (so that 'mini.ai' has precedence in defining mappings).",
    "closed_at": "2023-05-04T09:12:21Z",
