        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "In case anyone runs into this in the future, I've noticed that which-key will not display text objects if `i`/`a` are pressed before `timeoutlen` in visual mode. (Instead showing the `Enter ... textobject identifier (single character)` message) I believe this is due to the `vi`/`va` (or `V`/`C-v`) being read together and `getcharstr` being called which blocks, causing which-key to not display anything.\n\nI've worked around this by setting `timeoutlen` lower than the default `1000` to avoid the issue.\n\nThis also required me to use [better-escape.nvim](https://github.com/max397574/better-escape.nvim) to keep my \"jj\" binding working.\n\nEdit: I ended up with `timeoutlen` of 500 (mainly for [nvim-surround](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround?tab=readme-ov-file) to work) and kinda just accepted that if I want which-key for text objects, I have to first wait for which-key to popup for `y` first before pressing `i`/`a`. (I have which-key timeout set to 500 to be the same as `timeoutlen`, which makes the timing more clear.)",
