            "body": "> ... (Instead showing the `Enter ... textobject identifier (single character)` ...\n\nThis come from 'mini.ai' one second after user pressed `a` or `i`, not 'which-key.nvim'.\n\n> This also required me to use [better-escape.nvim](https://github.com/max397574/better-escape.nvim) to keep my \"jj\" binding working.\n\nThere is now similar functionality in 'mini.nvim', if you are interested: [`map_combo()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/473cdbff498ed120f1768c75ef65fa42859aa14f/doc/mini-keymap.txt#L140-L146) from 'mini.keymap'.",
